 you want a giant  pointy one that covers your whole chest  go for it the spider on the back is the  same deal but you have to cut it I have  some spare fabric since the leg pieces  of the red suit were still lying around  I printed off a stencil and cut it out  of that on top of a piece of foam I  pinned it to I am shocked by how well it  came out on my first try as always put  the seal and glue on the edges of  everything to make sure it doesn't fall  apart later after it settles slice it up  the middle so there's room for the  zipper and then glue the inside I kept a  full mat inside the suit in case it bled  through then up well up I guess it's  just done huh that was long and annoying  I didn't put the opening in the middle  by choice but I guess you could do that  if you want then add some buttons so it  snaps the two pieces together I'm kind  of surprised this was so doable I get  why he complains so much about replacing  these though making one of these suits  takes a while and doesn't allow you a  ton of free time but boy does it feel  cool to have it done Peter Parker had  the time and money to make web fluid in  high school he could probably do this  with more ease than I did  yes Peter Parker could absolutely make  his costume  would it look like $100,000 Hollywood  masterpiece sculpted by a team of  costume department experts nope it would  look more like this something charming  about the simplicity of it and now that  I've given you these hectic and  disorganized instructions you too can  live out childhood fantasies of running  across rooftops and getting stabbed by  muggers and dirty inner-city alleyways  or you can just make some cool cosplay  to wear while you go to comic book  conventions you giant nerd now if only I  knew how to make industrial-strength  glue that expands into rubber on contact  with oxygen I guess that'll be a later  video  [Music]
 

